    pr_ref:  # fc48
    description: "All Rust function_call edges resolve at 0.8 confidence by method name only, with no type disambiguation. Common names (.clone(), .build(), .get(), .filter(), .new(), .to_string()) produce massive false-positive fan-in. Examples: zed Source::clone has 6849 false in-edges, candle Tensor::get has 391 false callers, codex NetworkProxyBuilder::build has 20 false callers. This corrupts centrality rankings, reverse slices, and sketch selection for every Rust repo. Fixing requires type inference or at minimum receiver-type heuristics."  # fc48
    fields: {}  # fc48
